  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1131 AM MDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nUpper high will continue to spin over the Four Corners today and \ntomorrow allowing for hot and mostly dry conditions both days. The \nbest location for storms will be in the area mountains and western \nlocations bordering AZ. The hottest day of the week ahead will be \nTuesday where the lowlands will see highs in the upper 90s and low \ntriple digits. Some locations in the lower Valley may get close to \nHeat Advisory criteria (Max temp > or = 105F+), but not expecting a \nlarge area of 105F+. Locations along the Rio Grande Valley will be \nthe hottest locations with temperatures from 100F-104F. High \npressure will dissolve and rebuild over the Gulf States and the Gulf \nby Wednesday, allowing a slight uptick in storm activity and \ncoverage compared to Monday and Tuesday. Thursday and onward, it \nlooks like the area will be under a good monsoonal tap of moisture \nallowing for scattered mountain storms and isolated to scattered \nthunderstorms in the lowlands each afternoon. With the increase in \nmoisture, temperatures won't be quite as hot as Tuesday, but will be \na handful of degrees \"cooler\".",
